---
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the specification"
  description="How The Social Specification sources, scopes, and maintains social publishing requirements."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Standards,<br />not folklore.</h1>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        The Social Specification is an open reference for people and software that publish
        to social platforms.
      </p><h2>What belongs here</h2><p>
        Profile images, headers, biographies, post text, image and video dimensions, aspect
        ratios, file formats, file sizes, accessibility fields, attachment counts, and
        material differences between manual and API publishing.
      </p><h2>Source policy</h2><p>
        Stated limits require a first-party help page, developer document, or public
        protocol schema. If a current source cannot be found, the value is marked “Not
        documented.” Mastodon-style server configuration is marked “Instance-defined.”
      </p><h2>Contribute</h2><p>
        Platforms change frequently. Corrections and source updates are welcome on <a
          href="https://github.com/jdevalk/specification.social">GitHub</a
        >. Include a first-party URL and explain whether the rule applies to the user
        interface, API, or both.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
